L000419	
L000420	
L000421	
L000422	
L000423	The polar funnel forms as differential rotation winds the initially poloidal magnetic field,
L000424	producing a magnetically dominated region ($B^2/8\pi\rho_0\gtrsim1$) above the BH poles. The
L000425	resulting field geometry and velocities (Figs.~\ref{fig:final_outcome}–\ref{fig:A2_b2_over_2rho})
L000426	show a collimated outflow consistent with GRMHD simulations of tilted disks in fixed Kerr
L000427	backgrounds~\cite{Liska:2017alm,Liska:2019vne,2007ApJ...668..417F}. In our dynamical spacetime
L000428	the jets remain aligned with the BH spin rather than differentially precessing with the disk.
L000429	The morphology depends on spin orientation: A1 shows the cleanest collimation, A2–A3 broader funnels,
L000430	and A4 the most disrupted structure due to strong MRI-driven accretion and PPI activity.
L000431	Collimated outflows persist in all configurations, showing that even highly tilted self-gravitating
L000432	disks can accumulate horizon-threading flux and launch BZ jets,  making jet formation a robust
L000433	outcome of BHD systems across tilt angles and for  disk-to-BH mass ratios up to $\sim 30\%$.
L000434	
L000435	The EM luminosity is $\sim10^{54}\,\rm erg\,s^{-1}$ in all cases (Fig.~\ref{fig:PLuinosity}),
L000436	consistent with the BZ scaling $L_{\rm EM}\sim 10^{54}\chi_{0.9}^2M_{10^6}^2B_{10^{10}}^2\,{\rm erg
L000437	\,s^{-1}}$~\cite{1982MNRAS.199..883B}. The antialigned case exhibits the earliest and strongest peak,
L000438	coinciding with the rapid accretion phase that drives substantial spin-down.  This behavior reflects efficient
L000439	inward advection of magnetic flux during the MRI-enhanced accretion episode.  By contrast, the aligned
L000440	and moderately tilted cases maintain more stable luminosities consistent with their smoother accretion
L000441	histories.
L000442	
L000443	
L000444	
L000445	
L000446	
