L000796	\textit{Accretion.}\textemdash
L000797	
L000798	Fig.~\ref{fig:fig_accretion} shows the evolution of the rest-mass fraction outside
L000799	the apparent horizon and the corresponding accretion rate. The antialigned case (A4)
L000800	exhibits the earliest and most dramatic mass depletion: by $\sim 1\,P_c$ the mass
L000801	outside the horizon drops by nearly $30\%$, coincident with a sharp accretion peak.
L000802	This early onset reflects the short MRI growth time ($\tau_{\rm MRI}\sim 0.15\,P_c$),
L000803	which rapidly amplifies magnetic stresses. In A4, however,  the MRI interacts with
L000804	strong non axisymmetric structure: the $m=1$ mode grows significantly faster than
L000805	in the hydrodynamic counterpart
L000806	(see Fig.~4 in manuscript), {reaching large amplitudes within one orbital period and strongly distorting
L000807	the disk morphology}. The combined  action of MRI-driven turbulence and enhanced non
L000808	axisymmetric dynamics produces the violent accretion episode.
